    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0436" n="402" xml:id="pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">FE files, lot 55 D 128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commander in Chief
                        Far East (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-07-11T17:47:00-04:00">July 11, 1952—5:47
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>JCS 913383. From JCS.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Action you propose in para 6 C 51780<anchor n="1" xml:id="d218-f1"/> is
                        approved with understanding that method of presentation to Communists of new
                        round number of persons to be repatriated as outlined in part 1 CX
                            51489<anchor n="2" xml:id="d218-f2"/> should be modified as follows: <list>
                            <label>A.</label>
                            <item>Number of persons in each category should be presented only as
                                factual tabulation of results of completed UN screening. FYI this
                                approach will keep open possibility that there may be some increase
                                in total repatriated as result of some form of post armistice
                                interrogation.</item>
                            <label>B.</label>
                            <item>In reiterating proposals to permit individual interviews of
                                nonrepatriates ref should be made to an “impartial” rather than to a
                                “neutral” agency because of precedent established by our having
                                accepted Poland and Czechoslovakia as “neutrals” in Neutral Nations
                                Supervisory Commission. Use of word “impartial” would appear give us
                                greater negotiating latitude in arriving at an agency or group of
                                countries more acceptable to us for this purpose than one in which
                                there is satellite participation.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Decision on part 2 CX 51489 is being withheld pending development of
                        Communist reaction to foregoing presentation and outcome of discussions
                        between you and Gen Collins.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>There have been no further significant developments through
                            channels<anchor n="3" xml:id="d218-f3"/> referred to in JCS
                            911932.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d218-f4"/></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
